{#
  The FAQ section, once.

  It was written out four times — index.njk, painter-cairns.njk,
  painter-trinity-beach.njk and roof-painter-cairns.njk — eleven identical lines of
  markup in each, differing only in which list they read and two bits of wording.
  Four copies of one component is four places to fix a bug in, and they had already
  drifted: the roof page opens no question by default while the other three open the
  first one.

  ⚠️ THE EMPTY GUARD LIVES IN HERE ON PURPOSE. The heading sits outside the loop, so a
  list with nothing in it used to render "Have questions?" above blank space. Keeping
  the guard at the call sites meant repeating it four times and relying on whoever adds
  the fifth page to remember. Now there is nothing to remember.

  ⚠️ AND THE LEADING NEWLINE IS INSIDE THE GUARD, not outside it. A call site puts the
  comment, the set and the call all on one line, so this macro owns every byte of its
  own output: one newline then the section when there are questions, nothing at all
  when there are none. Moving that newline shifts a blank line into the built page.

  ⚠️ DO NOT WRITE A NUNJUCKS COMMENT TERMINATOR INSIDE THIS BLOCK. An earlier version of
  these notes spelled out a call site including the closing brace of a comment, which
  ended this comment three lines early and failed the whole build with "unexpected end
  of comment" — pointing at index.njk, not at this file.

  Usage, with the tokens spaced out so they cannot terminate this block:
    {% from "faq-section.njk" import faqSection %}   at the top of the page
    {{ faqSection(pageFaqs, "Have questions?", "FAQs related to …") }}
    {{ faqSection(pageFaqs, "Have questions?", "…", "background:var(--bg-soft)", false) }}
#}
{% macro faqSection(items, eyebrow, heading, style="", openFirst=true) %}{% if items | length %}
<section class="faq-block"{% if style %} style="{{ style }}"{% endif %}>
  <div class="wrap-narrow">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">{{ eyebrow }}</span>
      <h2>{{ heading }}</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">{% for f in items %}
      <details{% if openFirst and loop.first %} open{% endif %}>
        <summary>{{ f.q }} <span class="plus">+</span></summary>
        <div>{{ f.a }}</div>
      </details>{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
